1
00:00:07,478 --> 00:00:14,046
The button is in the same place on every
screen, because you do not go looking for

2
00:00:14,046 --> 00:00:16,209
it at seven in the morning.

3
00:00:16,659 --> 00:00:23,548
Where you are matters. The workspace has a
boundary, and the server checks it — not

4
00:00:23,548 --> 00:00:24,461
the screen.

5
00:00:24,916 --> 00:00:31,832
In. From here the day is being counted,
and nobody has to remember what time it

6
00:00:31,832 --> 00:00:32,532
started.

7
00:00:32,984 --> 00:00:38,297
The shift is on screen while it runs:
when it started, how long it has been, and

8
00:00:38,297 --> 00:00:39,161
what is left.

9
00:00:39,611 --> 00:00:46,902
Out at the end, and the record closes
itself. That record is what payroll reads.

10
00:00:47,355 --> 00:00:52,371
Every shift is kept, with where
it was and how it was recorded.

11
00:00:52,822 --> 00:00:58,792
Next: why the hours on that record and
the hours on a payslip are not the same

12
00:00:58,792 --> 00:01:01,088
number — and that being right.

